    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several favorable matchups tonight, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (73.00) leading our production projections. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Michael Wacha, where a +14% boost from dynamic platoon factors and a +12% bump due to the starter's xERA combine to make him our most potent engine for run production. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is a priority start; his ability to leverage a slow pitcher delivery into potential stolen bases\u2014our scarcest category\u2014coupled with a favorable +13% platoon adjustment against Andre Pallante, positions him as a high-floor, high-ceiling play despite a minor park penalty.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today\u2019s slate involved keeping **Gunnar Henderson** (58.38) on the bench. Despite his immense talent, he drew a difficult assignment against Logan Gilbert, whose elite 3.26 xERA severely hampered the scoring output in our model, resulting in a -18% SP Skill penalty that just barely knocked him out of the starting rotation behind more favorable platoon situations. Furthermore, managers should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci**; while both are currently projected for leadoff spots\u2014providing substantial value via plate appearance volume\u2014any late shifts down the order would trigger a meaningful downward revision to their efficiency scores. Finally, proceed with caution regarding **Kyle Tucker** (54.20); while his talent is undeniable, facing Drew Rasmussen carries significant risk, as the tough matchup suppressed his score enough that he barely clung to his spot in the outfield.",
